# Repos a reviewer of THIS repo may search and cite, materialized under
# .siblings/<owner>/<repo>. Declared rather than left to the fallback so the
# set is the one this repo actually depends on.
#
# One per line. The reviewer host must also carry a SOURCE_PATHS entry for
# each, or the sibling reports as `missing` and is never searched.
#
# Each row is a real edge: `plow-hermes-agent` is the base the Dockerfile
# builds FROM by digest, and it owns boot, `plow-init`, the gateway config
# seed this image overlays, and the SOUL.md recompose; `hermes-plugin-plow`
# is the `plow_chat` plugin that base pins, which frames every turn, and whose
# chat adapter `post_to_chat.py` mirrors call for call; `latch` owns the MCP
# tools and the gog grammar that research, calendar, mail and print drive;
# `agent-index-client` is pinned by commit and sha256 in `vendor/client.pin`;
# `plow-agents` owns the install contract and the compose shape `compose.yml`
# follows; `agent-mgr` still execs `deploy-hook` and reads `agent.env`.
#
# The two NousResearch rows are SUBTREES of upstream Hermes, because
# `image/hermes/patch_*.py` rewrite `gateway/run_turn.py`,
# `gateway/response_filters.py` and `agent/conversation_loop.py` at build: a
# reviewer of a patch needs the function it anchors on.
#
# `plow-pbc/plow` stays out although the chat and print scripts call its API:
# it is private and this repo is public, so a citation into it would publish
# private paths. `hermes-plugin-plow` makes the same API calls in public.

plow-pbc/plow-hermes-agent
plow-pbc/hermes-plugin-plow
plow-pbc/latch
plow-pbc/agent-index-client
plow-pbc/plow-agents
plow-pbc/agent-mgr
NousResearch/hermes-gateway
NousResearch/hermes-agent-core
